The plate looks like a dinner plate, but its rim is wide. The inner well is roughly 18 cm across and the outer diameter is about 26 cm. The lasagna piece measures about 8 x 7 cm and is about 4-5 cm tall, which gives a volume of roughly 250 cm³. Lasagna is dense, around 1 g/cm³, so I'd put it near 230 g. That is a bit high for a piece this size, so I settled on about 220 g.

Lasagna with meat sauce and cheese runs about 150-170 kcal/100 g. The tomato sauce on top and the sprinkled parmesan are already part of the lasagna value, so I did not list them separately.

